      "text": "We can set $y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}$. The equation then becomes $y^2 + y = 12$. \n\nWe can factor this equation as $y^2 + y - 12 = 0$ and solve for $y$. \n\nThe quadratic formula gives $y = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1^2 - 4(-12)(1)}}{2(1)} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2}$. \n\nSo, $y = \\frac{±7}{2}$. \n\nNow we can find the value of $x$ by undoing the original substitution. \n\nIf $y = \\frac{7}{2}$, then $\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = \\frac{7}{2}$, so $4x = \\frac{7(2)(3x-4)}{2}$. \n\nSimplifying this gives $x = \\boxed{\\frac{7}{4}}$. \n\nSimilarly, if $y = -\\frac{7}{2}$, then $\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -\\frac{7}{2}$, so $4x = -\\frac{7(2)(3x-4)}{2}$. \n\nSimplifying this gives $x = \\boxed{\\frac{34}{7}}$. \n\nTherefore, the greatest possible value of $x$ is $\\boxed{\\frac{34}{7}}$.The answer is: \\frac{34}{7}",
